        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'You are now the experts. Your job is to explain to a neighbour who thinks forecasts are useless.' Share the CER checklist on the board. Give 10 minutes of silent writing, then 5 minutes for peer review. Circulate and push with: 'Show me the number that supports that sentence.' and 'Which lesson gave you that idea?' Use cold-calls: choose 3 learners to read one sentence of evidence. Then pose the unlucky-day question and use WAIT TIME of 15 seconds. Cold-call 3 learners. Draw out the idea: 'A decision based on probability is judged over many days, not on one day.' Link to cost of being wrong: planting early risks losing seed if dry, while waiting risks missing the rains. Pilot: storm risk affects safety. County: flood risk to residents.",
