        "teacherMoves": "Open the DQB and say: 'Look at the questions we asked on Day 1. Which can you answer now? Show me the evidence.' Give groups 8 minutes for sorting. Ask: 'Which lesson helped you answer this one?' Then facilitate a 4-minute whole-class synthesis. Cold-call 4 learners, one per zone or question type. WAIT TIME 10-15 seconds. Model a strong answer: 'Probability is applied by measuring how likely events are from past records and rules, then comparing those probabilities with the cost of being wrong to decide.' Accept genuine open questions and explain that they are a sign of good science. Link back to KICD key inquiries: 'How do we determine the probability of an event?' (relative frequency and theoretical probability) and 'How do we apply probability in real life situations?' (decisions for the farmer, pilot and county).",
